-- Glossary terms of items, makes and mounts (see Data/Glossary.lua), hovered in the
-- blocks of the item browser, the crafting window and the stable. Kept apart from
-- the main glossary so new terms there and here don't touch each other's lines.
local _, ns = ...
local G = ns.Glossary

G["Attunement"] = "A bond with a magic item that asks for one. Until you are attuned, the item works only as a plain one of its kind would. Attuning takes a short rest spent with the item; you can be attuned to three items at a time, and to only one copy of the same item."
G["Consumable"] = "An item that is used up when used: a potion once drunk, a scroll once read, a piece of magic ammunition once it hits. It is worth half its rarity's price, and making one takes half the usual time and cost (a spell scroll goes by its own scribing rules)."
G["Harness"] = "An animal in harness pulls a cart, wagon, sled or chariot. It can move five times what it can carry, the vehicle's own weight included, and the animals of a team add their capacities together."
G["Make"] = "A magic version of a plain suit of armor, shield, weapon or piece of ammunition, such as a Flame Tongue longsword or a mithral chain shirt. It counts as the plain item with its magic on top, and costs the plain item's price plus what its rarity is worth."
